From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 00:10:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] pmdomain: apple: pmp-report: let t8132_gfx_request
 change at run time

The T8132 GFX power request (PS-REQ bit 12) is applied once at probe and
its parameter is read-only, so testing what it does to the rest of the
SoC needs a boot per setting. Single-thread memory latency on the J604
read 85-88 ns on trains before the request was added and 98-100 ns
since, and this is one of the memory-side changes in between.

Make the parameter writable: a write holds or drops the bit at once on
the T8132 report that was probed. The default stays on.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 drivers/pmdomain/apple/pmp-report.c | 29 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 26 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/pmdomain/apple/pmp-report.c b/drivers/pmdomain/apple/pmp-report.c
index 52369f0623..4a8d75cd81 100644
--- a/drivers/pmdomain/apple/pmp-report.c
+++ b/drivers/pmdomain/apple/pmp-report.c
@@ -504,15 +504,38 @@ static void apple_pmp_report_t8132_dvfs_trial(struct apple_pmp_report *rep)
  */
 #define PMP_T8132_GFX_REQUEST_BIT	12
 static bool t8132_gfx_request = true;
-module_param(t8132_gfx_request, bool, 0444);
+static struct apple_pmp_report *apple_pmp_t8132_rep;
+
+/* Writable at run time: a write holds or drops bit 12 at once on the probed T8132 report. */
+static int apple_pmp_t8132_gfx_request_set(const char *val, const struct kernel_param *kp)
+{
+	struct apple_pmp_report *rep = READ_ONCE(apple_pmp_t8132_rep);
+	int ret = param_set_bool(val, kp);
+
+	if (ret || !rep)
+		return ret;
+	ret = apple_pmp_report_set_state(rep, PMP_T8132_GFX_REQUEST_BIT, t8132_gfx_request, true);
+	dev_info(rep->dev, "t8132: GFX power request (PS-REQ bit %d) %s at run time: %d\n",
+		 PMP_T8132_GFX_REQUEST_BIT, t8132_gfx_request ? "held" : "dropped", ret);
+	return ret;
+}
+
+static const struct kernel_param_ops apple_pmp_t8132_gfx_request_ops = {
+	.set = apple_pmp_t8132_gfx_request_set,
+	.get = param_get_bool,
+};
+module_param_cb(t8132_gfx_request, &apple_pmp_t8132_gfx_request_ops, &t8132_gfx_request, 0644);
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(t8132_gfx_request,
-		 "T8132: hold the GFX power request (PS-REQ bit 12) as macOS does (default on; 0: bit 12 clear, as before)");
+		 "T8132: hold the GFX power request (PS-REQ bit 12) as macOS does (default on; 0: bit 12 clear, as before; writable at run time)");
 
 static void apple_pmp_report_t8132_gfx_request(struct apple_pmp_report *rep)
 {
 	int ret;
 
-	if (rep->offsets != &apple_pmp_offsets_t8132 || !t8132_gfx_request)
+	if (rep->offsets != &apple_pmp_offsets_t8132)
+		return;
+	WRITE_ONCE(apple_pmp_t8132_rep, rep);
+	if (!t8132_gfx_request)
 		return;
 	ret = apple_pmp_report_set_state(rep, PMP_T8132_GFX_REQUEST_BIT, true, true);
 	if (ret)
-- 
